rds.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"entry_points\": [\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n      \"kind\": \"console_script\",\n      \"source\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n      \"kind\": \"API registration\",\n      \"source\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"POST /orders\",\n      \"kind\": \"HTTP API\",\n      \"handler\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"identifier\": \"GET /orders/<order_id>\",\n      \"kind\": \"HTTP API\",\n      \"handler\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dependency_edges\": [\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\", \"type\": \"imports\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"to\": \"MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY\", \"type\": \"reads_config\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\", \"type\": \"instantiates\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"type\": \"calls\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\", \"to\": \"SQLite orders table\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"to\": \"SQLite orders table\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"},\n    {\"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"to\": \"SQLite orders table\", \"type\": \"persists_to\"}\n  ],\n  \"key_functions\": [\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\", \"importance\": \"Process entry point; wires configuration and storage, initializes schema, and returns 0.\", \"behavior\": \"Reads os.environ indirectly through load_settings; does not start an HTTP server or enforce readonly.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\", \"importance\": \"Defines runtime database location and readonly setting.\", \"behavior\": \"MINISVC_DB defaults to orders.sqlite; MINISVC_READONLY is true only for value 1.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\", \"importance\": \"Write boundary for new orders.\", \"behavior\": \"Opens SQLite and inserts one Order; duplicate IDs and database errors propagate.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\", \"importance\": \"Read boundary for orders.\", \"behavior\": \"Queries by order_id and returns Order or None.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\", \"importance\": \"HTTP adapter registration boundary.\", \"behavior\": \"Registers POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id> using lambdas.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\", \"importance\": \"Create-order application handler.\", \"behavior\": \"Indexes required payload keys, converts total_cents with int, saves once, and returns a generated event.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\", \"importance\": \"Read-order application handler.\", \"behavior\": \"Returns missing or serialized order response and generates a read event.\"},\n    {\"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\", \"importance\": \"Audit-shaped response event builder.\", \"behavior\": \"Returns a dictionary only; no table, file, or logging sink is used.\"}\n  ],\n  \"runtime_flows\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"CLI startup\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"Console script minisvc invokes minisvc.cli:main.\",\n        \"main calls load_settings(os.environ).\",\n        \"load_settings selects MINISVC_DB or orders.sqlite and parses MINISVC_READONLY.\",\n        \"main constructs OrderRepository(settings.database_path).\",\n        \"main calls repo.init_schema(), creating SQLite table orders if absent.\",\n        \"main prints readiness and returns 0.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n      \"steps\": [\n        \"An application calls register_routes(app, repo).\",\n        \"POST /orders dispatches through the registered lambda to create_order(payload, repo).\",\n        \"create_order reads order_id, customer, and total_cents and converts total_cents with int().\",\n        \"create_order constructs an Order and calls repo.save(order), which inserts into SQLite once.\",\n        \"create_order calls order_event(order, created) to build an in-memory event.\",\n        \"The handler returns status created, order_id, and event; no audit record is persisted.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"},"intent":"Create module map JSON"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":781,"output":2018,"cacheRead":19200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21999,"cost":{"input":0.0001562,"output":0.0024216,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0029617999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788149302173,"responseId":"resp_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe366d0087d282231c4efe077472","duration":37342.944467999994,"ttft":1126.4442500000005},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YgeQM0TXBfpy5vhNW0JtygvE|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe37430487d2a6f4a8e1e0a84dc8","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/module_map.json#345E]\nSuccessfully wrote 6808 bytes to out/module_map.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/module_map.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788149339555},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe5e2cec87d28b60e38255431164\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_UzpkyaSagvu7f7m7rrJNjf8S|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe5e81ac87d2a0499f95bbb66ee3","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write architecture summary","path":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","content":"# minisvc architecture\n\n## Scope\n\n`minisvc` is a small order service with a console bootstrap and an HTTP adapter. The fixture README says the code is authoritative when the older design notes disagree. `minisvc/__init__.py`, `minisvc/api/__init__.py`, and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package marker/export files, not business-logic modules; the active runtime is in the seven Python modules below.\n\n## Modules\n\n- **`minisvc.cli` (`minisvc/cli.py`)** — console-script entry point. Loads settings, constructs `OrderRepository`, initializes the schema, prints readiness, and returns zero. It does not launch an HTTP server.\n- **`minisvc.config` (`minisvc/config.py`)** — frozen `Settings` dataclass plus `load_settings`. Reads `MINISVC_DB` (default `orders.sqlite`) and `MINISVC_READONLY` (`\"1\"` means true).\n- **`minisvc.models` (`minisvc/models.py`)** — `Order` dataclass with `order_id`, `customer`, and integer `total_cents`.\n- **`minisvc.storage.repo` (`minisvc/storage/repo.py`)** — SQLite repository. `init_schema` creates `orders`; `save` inserts; `get` selects by ID. Each operation opens its own SQLite connection with a context manager.\n- **`minisvc.api.routes` (`minisvc/api/routes.py`)** — registers `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/<order_id>` against an injected `app` and repository.\n- **`minisvc.api.handlers` (`minisvc/api/handlers.py`)** — application handlers. `create_order` maps a payload to an `Order`, saves it, and returns a response event. `get_order` maps a repository result to either a missing or successful response.\n- **`minisvc.audit` (`minisvc/audit.py`)** — constructs an order event dictionary. Despite its name, it has no persistence or logging sink.\n\n## Entry points\n\nThe packaging entry point is `minisvc = minisvc.cli:main` in `pyproject.toml`. API setup is `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`; it binds `POST /orders` to `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` and `GET /orders/<order_id>` to `get_order`. The HTTP framework is intentionally abstract: `register_routes` expects an `app` exposing `post` and `get`, plus an injected repository.\n\n## Data flow\n\n### CLI startup\n\n`minisvc.cli:main` → `load_settings(os.environ)` → `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)` → `repo.init_schema()` → readiness print. `readonly` is loaded into `Settings` but is not consulted by `main` or the repository.\n\n### HTTP create order\n\n`register_routes(app, repo)` installs a POST callback → `create_order(payload, repo)` indexes `order_id` and `customer`, converts `total_cents` using `int`, and constructs `Order` → `OrderRepository.save` inserts into SQLite → `order_event(order, \"created\")` builds a dictionary → response returns `status`, `order_id`, and the event. There is no retry loop and no separate audit write.\n\nThe read path is analogous: `GET /orders/<order_id>` → `get_order` → `repo.get`; a missing row returns `status: missing`, otherwise the `Order` dataclass dictionary and an in-memory `read` event are returned.\n\n## Storage\n\nThe only durable store is the SQLite database at `Settings.database_path`, defaulting to a relative `orders.sqlite` in the process working directory. The `orders` table has a primary key `order_id`, required `customer`, and required integer `total_cents`. `save` relies on SQLite errors for duplicate IDs and other failures; it does not implement retries, transactions spanning multiple operations, or durability configuration beyond SQLite defaults. Events returned by `order_event` are transient response data, not rows in an audit table.\n\n## Risks and extension points\n\n- **Readonly gap:** `MINISVC_READONLY=1` currently changes configuration state only; `create_order` can still call `save`, and CLI startup still calls `init_schema`. Enforce the policy at the application/repository write boundary and decide whether schema initialization is allowed.\n- **Input validation:** missing payload keys raise `KeyError`; malformed `total_cents` raises `ValueError`; no checks enforce non-empty strings, non-negative totals, bounds, or unknown-field policy. Add an explicit request validation layer and map failures to stable HTTP errors.\n- **Failure handling:** `save` is one attempt. Duplicate IDs and SQLite operational errors propagate through the handler. Add narrowly scoped retry policy only for retryable database errors, with idempotency handling for repeated creates.\n- **Audit semantics:** `order_event` is response shaping, not an audit trail. If auditability is required, define an append-only schema/sink, atomicity with the order write, and retention/access controls.\n- **Runtime environment:** relative database paths depend on the current working directory, and `main` does not start an HTTP adapter. Deployment integration must supply an app/server lifecycle and an explicit database path.\n\nThe clean extension seams are `Settings` for runtime configuration, `OrderRepository` for persistence, `register_routes` for framework binding, and the handler functions for validation and application policy.\n"},"intent":"Write architecture summary"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2828,"output":1216,"cacheRead":19200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23244,"reasoningTokens":8,"cost":{"input":0.0005656000000000001,"output":0.0014592,"cacheRead":0.000384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0024088}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788149339581,"responseId":"resp_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe5bd53c87d2b4a24dde011aba7e","duration":24618.60211899999,"ttft":2632.931926999998},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_UzpkyaSagvu7f7m7rrJNjf8S|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe5e81ac87d2a0499f95bbb66ee3","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/architecture.md#AB61]\nSuccessfully wrote 4986 bytes to out/architecture.md"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788149364207},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe7513d887d2802b92c06bddf9b7\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_IPAgzk5a1CQ78pkNmyFTUoln|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe75d71087d290764caa616eea77","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write documentation discrepancy CSV","path":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","content":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 parses readonly into Settings, but minisvc/cli.py:8-10 still initializes schema and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 always calls OrderRepository.save; no code checks settings.readonly\",\"contradicted\",\"Writes remain possible while readonly is configured, creating an unsafe false assurance.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) exactly once; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 has one sqlite insert and no retry loop or error response conversion\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures propagate and callers receive no documented retry behavior.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns a dictionary; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only orders and contains no audit table or audit insert\",\"contradicted\",\"Returned events can be lost and cannot support durable audit or compliance requirements.\"\n\"The service accepts orders through a small HTTP adapter and a CLI bootstrap command\",\"README.md:3\",\"pyproject.toml:6-7 defines the CLI script; minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 registers POST /orders and GET /orders/<order_id>\",\"confirmed\",\"The documented integration surfaces are present, although the HTTP framework/server lifecycle is injected rather than implemented here.\"\n"},"intent":"Write documentation discrepancy CSV"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2025,"output":406,"cacheRead":21248,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23679,"reasoningTokens":33,"cost":{"input":0.00040500000000000003,"output":0.00048719999999999997,"cacheRead":0.00042496,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00131716}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788149364211,"responseId":"resp_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe74acb087d2b12a8dac79d3df55","duration":8243.920121999996,"ttft":901.5572169999941},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_IPAgzk5a1CQ78pkNmyFTUoln|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe75d71087d290764caa616eea77","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv#7612]\nSuccessfully wrote 1476 bytes to out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788149372462},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe7d34cc87d2a85ecbe1755bdb7d\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_WKneHyENqzQPPpiBQYy244r1|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe7da4a087d29bad56485e804ece","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write risk register CSV","path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","content":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR-001,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:12-15 and :17-22 use SQLite with relative database_path; no backup, journal, migration, or durability policy is configured\",\"Data can be written to an unexpected working-directory file and recovery guarantees are undefined.\",\"Require an explicit deployment path, define SQLite durability/backup policy, and add migration/version handling.\",\"Platform/storage owner\"\nR-002,audit behavior,\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 order_event returns a dict; minisvc/api/handlers.py:13 and :20 place it only in the response; repo.py has no audit table\",\"Audit history disappears after the response and cannot provide an independent tamper-resistant record.\",\"Define an append-only audit sink/table and make order plus audit write atomic where required.\",\"Application/data owner\"\nR-003,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 defaults to relative orders.sqlite and parses readonly; cli.py:8-11 does not enforce readonly and does not start an HTTP server\",\"Environment drift can select the wrong database; readonly deployments still permit writes; a CLI-ready process may be mistaken for an HTTP service.\",\"Make database path explicit, enforce readonly at write/schema boundaries, and document or implement server lifecycle integration.\",\"Runtime/platform owner\"\nR-004,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-11 directly indexes payload keys and calls int(payload['total_cents']) with no schema or range checks\",\"Malformed or missing input raises KeyError/ValueError, while negative, huge, empty, or extra values are not governed by a contract.\",\"Add explicit payload validation, bounds and business rules, and stable client error mapping before constructing Order.\",\"API owner\"\nR-005,write failure handling,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 perform one insert; duplicate primary keys and SQLite errors propagate\",\"Transient failures are not retried and duplicate submissions have no explicit idempotency response.\",\"Classify retryable errors, add bounded retry/backoff where safe, and define idempotency/duplicate-ID semantics.\",\"Application/storage owner\"\nR-006,access control,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 registers public-looking order routes without authentication, authorization, or rate limiting\",\"Any upstream-exposed caller may read or create orders unless the hosting adapter supplies controls.\",\"Specify the trust boundary and add authentication, authorization, and request limits at the adapter or service boundary.\",\"Service/security owner\"\n"},"intent":"Write risk register CSV"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1444,"output":602,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24318,"reasoningTokens":14,"cost":{"input":0.0002888,"output":0.0007224,"cacheRead":0.00044544,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0014566400000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788149372466,"responseId":"resp_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe7cd5a087d2b3f4d2a326bb75f6","duration":11716.028816999999,"ttft":793.0631909999938},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_WKneHyENqzQPPpiBQYy244r1|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe7da4a087d29bad56485e804ece","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/risk_register.csv#1824]\nSuccessfully wrote 2588 bytes to out/risk_register.csv"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788149384188},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe8ab69487d2a7f2caec5510338d\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"},\"summary\":[],\"metadata\":{\"turn_id\":\"f1af01fe-3361-445c-83d4-fdbc84b8677b\"}}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_VYeiExJhiPfpI4zhqMuY0kYk|fc_0a3f42478cd969d4016a94fe8d60b087d2b487b3b540e6a6d4","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Write onboarding plan","path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","content":"# minisvc onboarding plan\n\n## Recommended read order\n\n1. `README.md` and `pyproject.toml` — stated behavior and the `minisvc.cli:main` console entry point. Treat the README design notes as claims to verify, not as authority.\n2. `minisvc/config.py` — `Settings` and environment parsing.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` — startup wiring and the actual process lifecycle.\n4. `minisvc/models.py` — the small `Order` domain object.\n5. `minisvc/storage/repo.py` — SQLite schema and repository boundaries.\n6. `minisvc/api/routes.py`, then `minisvc/api/handlers.py` — HTTP binding and create/read behavior.\n7. `minisvc/audit.py` — response event construction and its lack of persistence.\n\nThe three `__init__.py` files are package markers (the root one has a small `__all__` export list); they are not active request or storage logic.\n\n## Run and smoke-test locally\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -e .\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-onboarding.sqlite minisvc\n```\n\nThe command creates the `orders` table if needed and prints readiness. It does not start an HTTP server. A direct handler smoke test can exercise the active path without a framework:\n\n```bash\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc-onboarding.sqlite python - <<'PY'\nfrom minisvc.api.handlers import create_order, get_order\nfrom minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n\nrepo = OrderRepository(\"/tmp/minisvc-onboarding.sqlite\")\nrepo.init_schema()\nprint(create_order({\"order_id\": \"demo-1\", \"customer\": \"Ada\", \"total_cents\": \"1250\"}, repo))\nprint(get_order(\"demo-1\", repo))\nPY\n```\n\nThere are no test files or test dependency declarations in this fixture. Until a suite is added, use the smoke path above and manually exercise missing keys, invalid totals, duplicate IDs, and `MINISVC_READONLY=1` to observe current behavior.\n\n## First debugging trace point\n\nSet the first breakpoint at `minisvc.api.handlers.create_order` line 6. Trace payload extraction and `int()` conversion, then step into `OrderRepository.save` line 17 to observe the SQLite insert. For startup/configuration issues, use `minisvc.cli.main` line 8 and inspect `settings.readonly` versus the subsequent unconditional schema initialization.\n\n## Safe first changes\n\n1. Add focused request validation immediately before `Order(...)` in `create_order`, with explicit handling for missing keys, integer conversion, non-negative totals, and stable client-facing errors. Preserve the repository interface and add behavior tests for invalid and valid payloads.\n2. Enforce readonly at 